-----Original Message-----
From: RouteWise Support <routewise@routewise.example>
Sent: Monday, 12 October 2026 11:15
To: Tom Hendriks
Subject: Re: TMS upgrade to RouteWise 9.2 - weekend 24-25 Oct

Thanks for the clear description. RW-48213 is confirmed: the stop surcharge w=
as indeed applied from the first drop instead of from the second. Fix is incl=
uded in build 9.2.0.3. RW-48217: the CO2 value is calculated, but not written=
 to legs 2 and 3 because of a mapping bug in the reporting table. Same build =
fixes it. We will install 9.2.0.3 on RW-QA on 16 October. Production will get=
 9.2.0.3 directly during the weekend upgrade, so no extra downtime.

Best regards,
RouteWise Support
TMS software vendor

-----Original Message-----
From: Tom Hendriks <t.hendriks@corp-europe.example>
Sent: Thursday, 08 October 2026 09:30
To: RouteWise Support
Subject: RE: TMS upgrade to RouteWise 9.2 - weekend 24-25 Oct

We finished the first test run on RW-QA. 38 of 40 cases are fine, but we foun=
d two defects. 1) Multi-stop rate calculation (TC-017): a 3-drop route is cal=
culated at EUR 612.40 where our contract tariff gives EUR 584.90. It looks li=
ke the stop surcharge is applied to the first drop as well. 2) CO2 field (TC-=
033): empty for the second and third leg of multi-leg shipments. We logged th=
em as tickets RW-48213 (rate) and RW-48217 (CO2). Please tell us if a fix is =
possible before 24 October, otherwise we need to discuss go or no-go.

Thanks,
Tom Hendriks
Transport planner
Corp Europe B.V. | Rotterdam
T +31 10 579 9850

This e-mail and any attachments are confidential and intended solely for the =
addressee. If you received it in error, please delete it.

-----Original Message-----
From: RouteWise Support <routewise@routewise.example>
Sent: Wednesday, 23 September 2026 10:05
To: Tom Hendriks
Subject: TMS upgrade to RouteWise 9.2 - weekend 24-25 Oct

Following our call yesterday, we confirm the upgrade of your production TMS f=
rom 9.0 to 9.2 for the weekend of 24-25 October. The window runs from Saturda=
y 06:00 to Sunday 14:00 CET. Your QA system RW-QA will be upgraded to 9.2.0.2=
 by us on 5 October, so you have about three weeks for testing. Main changes:=
 new multi-stop rate engine, extended CO2 reporting per shipment leg and a ne=
w REST API version. Please note the old API v2 stays available, so existing i=
ntegrations should keep working, but we recommend testing them. Can you send =
us your test plan before the QA upgrade?

Best regards,
RouteWise Support
TMS software vendor

